  "description": "Use cases for .NET apps with several clients (HTTP endpoints, MCP tools, gRPC services, jobs): a record implementing IUseCase, a handler implementing IUseCaseHandler<TUseCase, TResult, TError> and returning Hlibz.Results' Result<TResult, TError> (the value, or one of the errors it declares, a C# union of error types), and every client injecting the handler's own interface. A source generator lists the handlers at compile time (no assembly scan) and wraps each one in a pipeline that validates the use case against its DataAnnotations first, the same rules ASP.NET Core's validation applies (nested records, collections, record parameter attributes, IValidatableObject), with no ASP.NET Core dependency, then runs your own filters. Custom validation attributes can describe themselves (IDescribedRule, [RuleSummary]) for OpenAPI or tool schemas to publish.",
